Yes. There is a better approach than the one we were converging on.

The frontier work points toward a **compiler/runtime architecture**, not an SVG-animation library. SVG, Lottie, MP4 and even the stick man should all be replaceable outputs. The irreplaceable asset is the structured ritual itself.

The strongest signal across the recent literature is remarkably consistent: flat graphics are the wrong abstraction. September's Compositional SVG work argues for hierarchical, semantically meaningful objects; Vector Prism found that recovering semantic groups before asking a VLM to animate them dramatically improves motion coherence; VAnim goes further and represents animation as sparse state updates to persistent identified objects rather than regenerating frames. [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.14657?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

