# This follows VAnim's strongest idea

VAnim's central insight is that vector animation should be **sparse state changes over a persistent object tree** rather than full regenerated frames. It reports >9.8× sequence compression while preserving object identity and topology. [Proceedings of Machine Learning Research](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v306/liang26w.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

We don't need their model.

We should steal the abstraction.

Our version:

```text
STATE 0
operator.orientation = north
dagger.attach = hand.R
pentagram.visible = 0%

Δ STATE
operator.orientation = east

Δ STATE
arm.R.pose = trace.start

Δ STATE
pentagram.visible = 16%

Δ STATE
pentagram.visible = 32%
```

Most ritual animation is inherently sparse.

Perfect match.

