# And Vector Prism validates semantic IDs

Vector Prism's CVPR 2026 pipeline is essentially:

```text
SVG
→ semantic decomposition
→ motion planning
→ animation
```

because raw SVG paths do not tell the animator what objects mean. [Open Access CVF](https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2026/html/Yun_Vector_Prism_Animating_Vector_Graphics_by_Stratifying_Semantic_Structure_CVPR_2026_paper.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

We can do better because **we know semantics before creating the SVG**.

We don't need to rediscover:

```text
these six paths appear to form a right arm
```

We created:

```xml
<g id="operator.arm.right">
```

from the beginning.

That's a huge advantage.

