# The renderer must be deterministic

This is the biggest practical recommendation I would make for the YouTube ambition.

**Do not build a separate web animation renderer and video renderer.**

Build one renderer with:

```ts
render(scene, score, time)
```

The browser uses:

```text
time = live clock
```

The video exporter uses:

```text
time = frame_number / fps
```

So:

```text
WEB:
render(t = currentTime)
```

and:

```text
YOUTUBE:
render(0 / 30)
render(1 / 30)
render(2 / 30)
...
→ PNG/WebP frames
→ FFmpeg
```

Same renderer.

Exact same result.

This eliminates an enormous future maintenance problem.

