# Historical diagrams should enter through a separate route

The last two weeks of research strengthen this part substantially.

Back2Struct, released September 29, reconstructs diagrams into **object-level SVG/XML containing explicit shapes, text, topology and layout** instead of merely tracing pixels. [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.37016?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

That gives us:

```text
historic magician's table
        ↓
   page crop
        ↓
 Back2Struct
        ↓
semantic diagram
```

while engraving-like art goes:

```text
woodcut / seal / illustration
        ↓
      VTracer
        ↓
faithful path reconstruction
```

VTracer is still actively improving; its September 2.x changes specifically improve small-circle tracing, relevant to this material. [GitHub](https://github.com/visioncortex/vtracer/releases?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

For AI-based image→SVG, newer work such as HiVG is also worth testing as an optional adapter; its model uses hierarchical SVG tokenization rather than simply dumping flat paths. [GitHub](https://github.com/ximinng/HiVG?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Again: none of these becomes canonical.

They are ingestion engines.

