# LiveSVG goes in the embellishment layer

Do not use a video model to determine where an operator's hand goes during the LBRP.

We know that exactly.

Use deterministic rigging.

But later, LiveSVG is perfect for:

- robes moving;
- candle flames;
- smoke;
- hair;
- cloth;
- feathers;
- subtle breathing;
- atmospheric entities.

LiveSVG's approach first produces a target motion video and then fits existing SVG geometry to it using group transformations plus Bézier deformation. [Google Research](https://research.google/pubs/livesvg-zero-shot-svg-animation-via-video-generation/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

So:

```text
SEMANTIC MOTION
our engine
