# But I'd distinguish three semantic roles

This becomes very useful:

```text
actor.operator
actor.demonstrator
actor.guide
```

### Operator

The person actually doing the ritual.

Usually **you**.

### Demonstrator

Shows the physical actions.

Default:

```text
Thoth
```

Could instead be:

```text
user avatar
```

### Guide / Familiar

Doesn't necessarily mimic human gestures.

It can:

- narrate;
- point;
- move toward the correct direction;
- hover beside an object;
- illuminate a symbol;
- remind you of the next step;
- announce timing;
- demonstrate visualization;
- appear in videos.

That solves an important problem.

A user might generate:

```text
black cat
owl
tiny dragon
floating sphere
angelic machine
crow
strange abstract entity
```

which obviously cannot perform:

```text
touch forehead with right hand
```

But it can still **guide the ritual**.

