# What about lightweight flames / effects?

This is another reason SVG-first wins.

For the core ritual experience, do:
- SVG paths for geometry
- CSS/WAAPI for line drawing / glow
- small procedural flame loops
- simple smoke curves
- light pulses
- aura halos
- text fade-ins
- directional glows

These can look really nice and remain lightweight.

For example:
- pentagram traces in glowing dark green / pale gold
- flames flicker with a 2–3-frame looping distortion
- incense uses looping Bézier smoke
- archangel quarters use subtle icon/light overlays
- divine names appear briefly then dim

That gets you 80% of the magic feeling for 10% of the cost.

